    "When we talk about “signals” in an online evaluation of a chatbot, we’re really just referring to pieces of information that tell us how the system is performing.",
    "The course material points out that there are two broad categories of these signals: computed signals and captured signals.",
    "A computed signal is something you have to derive yourself.",
    "The raw data isn’t already there in a ready‑to‑use form; you need to do a little calculation or inference to turn it into a useful metric.",
    "The context doesn’t give a concrete example, but the key idea is that you’re actively processing the data to produce the signal.",
    "A captured signal, on the other hand, is already present in the interaction and you simply record it.",
    "No extra math or inference is required—you just take the value as it is and store it.",
    "Thumbs‑up or thumbs‑down feedback that a user clicks during a conversation is an example of a captured signal.",
    "Latency, which is the amount of time the chatbot takes to generate a particular answer, is a captured signal.",
    "Cost per conversation, such as the number of tokens used or the monetary cost incurred, is a captured signal.",
    "Those figures are already computed by the platform’s usage tracking, so you just capture and log them.",
    "Captured signals are the “already‑there” data points you log.",
    "Computed signals are the “need‑to‑derive” metrics you calculate yourself.",
    "Both types are important for a complete online evaluation.",
    "They together give you a picture of user satisfaction (thumbs feedback), system efficiency (latency), and resource usage (cost).",
    "You might compute additional performance indicators yourself."
] 

