    "Vibe testing is a very informal way of checking an LLM‑based application.",
    "In practice you just fire off a handful of prompts—usually five to ten—look at the answers, and decide “it feels right” or “it feels wrong.”",
    "The judgment is based on a gut feeling rather than any systematic metric.",
    "Because the prompts you choose are arbitrary, the test is not repeatable: a different set of questions a few days later might give a different impression.",
    "This approach is useful for a quick, personal sanity check, but it never produces a production‑ready assessment.",
    "The decision is made by feel, not by objective criteria.",
    "A developer might think the answers are correct simply because they match expectations, even if the model is hallucinating or missing edge cases.",
    "Because the prompts are chosen on the fly, you can’t reliably reproduce the test.",
    "If a bug appears later, you can’t trace it back to a specific test case.",
    "Five or ten questions cover only a tiny slice of the possible user interactions.",
    "Real users will ask a far wider variety of questions, and the model may behave unpredictably on those unseen inputs.",
    "Vibe testing doesn’t expose systematic failures such as bias, safety violations, or policy breaches.",
