Statements:
[
    "The MMLU benchmark is a large‑scale knowledge‑testing dataset that was introduced in September 2020.",
    "It contains roughly 14,000 multiple‑choice questions spread across about 57 different subjects.",
    "The subjects range from exams like the USMLE, USGRE, and AP to other academic domains.",
    "Each question is a standard MCQ with four answer options.",
    "The idea behind MMLU is to measure how much breadth of world knowledge a language model has.",
    "Researchers can gauge a model’s overall knowledge coverage by sending the entire set of questions to an LLM and recording the percentage of correct answers.",
    "Because the questions are publicly available, later generations of models can inadvertently learn them during training.",
    "This leads to contamination and eventual saturation of the benchmark.",
    "MMLU has been a foundational benchmark for evaluating the knowledge capabilities of large language models."
] 

